.TH pathchk 1 (date) "GNU coreutils (unreleased)"
.SH NAME
pathchk \- check whether file names are valid or portable
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY pathchk
.RI [ OPTION \~.\|.\|.\&]
.IR NAME \~.\|.\|.\&
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" Add any additional description here
.PP
Diagnose invalid or non\-portable file names.
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#pathchk-p
\fB\-p\fP
.UE
check for most POSIX systems
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#pathchk-P
\fB\-P\fP
.UE
check for empty names and leading "\-"
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#pathchk--portability
\fB\-\-portability\fP
.UE
check for all POSIX systems (equivalent to \fB\-p\fR \fB\-P\fR)
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/pathchk#pathchk--help
\fB\-\-help\fP
.UE
display this help and exit
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/pathchk#pathchk--version
\fB\-\-version\fP
.UE
output version information and exit
.SH AUTHOR
Written by Paul Eggert, David MacKenzie, and Jim Meyering.
